@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
# API_KEY and ADMIN_API_KEY are loaded from .env by VS Code REST Client.

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Add a document
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/documents
X-Api-Key: {{$dotenv ADMIN_API_KEY}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "externalId": "refund-policy",
  "title": "Refund Policy",
  "content": "Refunds are available within seven days."
}

### Replace the same document (the documentId should stay the same)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/documents
X-Api-Key: {{$dotenv ADMIN_API_KEY}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "externalId": "refund-policy",
  "title": "Refund Policy",
  "content": "Refunds are available within fourteen days."
}

### List documents
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/documents
X-Api-Key: {{$dotenv ADMIN_API_KEY}}

### Ask a question
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ask
X-Api-Key: {{$dotenv API_KEY}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Can I get a refund?"
}

### Ask a question that may not exist in context
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ask
X-Api-Key: {{$dotenv API_KEY}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Do you offer phone support?"
}

### Delete a document (replace 1 with an ID returned by the add request)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/documents/1
X-Api-Key: {{$dotenv ADMIN_API_KEY}}
